#: backtrace.cpp:83
msgid "Could not generate a backtrace as the debugger '%1' was not found."
msgstr "De Fehlerspoor natogahn is unmööglich, denn de Debugger '%1' is nich to finnen."

#: debugger.cpp:65
msgid "C&opy"
msgstr "K&opeern"

#: debugger.cpp:82
msgid "Done."
msgstr "Fardig."

#: debugger.cpp:102
#, c-format
msgid "Backtrace saved to %1"
msgstr "Fehlerspoor in %1 afspiekert"

#: debugger.cpp:106
msgid "Cannot create a file in which to save the backtrace"
msgstr "De Datei für de Fehlerspoor kann nich maakt warrn"

#: debugger.cpp:111
msgid "Select Filename"
msgstr "Dateinaam utsöken"

#: debugger.cpp:119
msgid "A file named \"%1\" already exists. Are you sure you want to overwrite it?"
msgstr "Een Datei mit den Naam \"%1\" gifft dat al. Wullt Du dat redig överschrieven?"

#: debugger.cpp:121
msgid "Overwrite File?"
msgstr "Datei överschrieven?"

#: debugger.cpp:122
msgid "&Overwrite"
msgstr "&Överschrieven"

#: debugger.cpp:134
msgid "Cannot open file %1 for writing"
msgstr "Schrieven is nich mööglich. De Datei %1 lett sik nich opmaken"

#: debugger.cpp:142
msgid "Unable to create a valid backtrace."
msgstr "Een gellen Fehlerspoor lett sik nich opstellen."

#: debugger.cpp:143
msgid ""
"This backtrace appears to be of no use.\n"
"This is probably because your packages are built in a way which prevents "
"creation of proper backtraces, or the stack frame was seriously corrupted in "
"the crash.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"As dat lett is de Fehlerspoor nich to'n Bruken wesen.\n"
"Dien Programmen sünd wull so buut, dat dat Maken vun Fehlerspooren nich geiht, "
"oder bi't Afstörten is de Befehlsstapel (stack frame) ramponeert worrn.\n"
"\n"

#: debugger.cpp:152
msgid "Loading backtrace..."
msgstr "Fehlerspoor ward opstellt..."

#: debugger.cpp:175
msgid ""
"The following options are enabled:\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Disse Optschonen sünd anmaakt:\n"
"\n"

#: debugger.cpp:177
msgid ""
"\n"
"As the usage of these options is not recommended - because they can, in rare "
"cases, be responsible for KDE problems - a backtrace will not be generated.\n"
"You need to turn these options off and reproduce the problem again in order to "
"get a backtrace.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Dat Bruken vun disse Optschonen kann enkeltwies to Problemen mit KDE föhren, "
"ehr Bruuk is nich anraadt, un en Fehlerspoor warrt nich maakt.\n"
"Wenn Du en Fehlerspoor bruukst, muttst Du de Optschonen utmaken un dat Problem "
"noch maal reproduzeren.\n"

#: debugger.cpp:182
msgid "Backtrace will not be created."
msgstr "En Fehlerspoor warrt nich maakt."

#: debugger.cpp:190
msgid "Loading symbols..."
msgstr "An't Laden vun den Symbolen..."

#: debugger.cpp:212
msgid "System configuration startup check disabled.\n"
msgstr "Pröven vun't Systeem bi't Starten is utmaakt.\n"

#: drbugreport.cpp:54
msgid "You have to edit the description before the report can be sent."
msgstr "Ehr de Bericht sennt ward muttst du'n Beschrieven ingeven."

#: krashconf.cpp:74
msgid "unknown"
msgstr "unbekannt"

#: main.cpp:43
msgid "KDE crash handler gives the user feedback if a program crashed"
msgstr "De KDE Afstörten-Pleeger vertellt den Bruker wat vun den Afstört"

#: main.cpp:47
msgid "The signal number that was caught"
msgstr "De faatkregen Signaalnummer"

#: main.cpp:48
msgid "Name of the program"
msgstr "Naam vun't Programm"

#: main.cpp:49
msgid "Path to the executable"
msgstr "Padd to de utföhrbaare Datei"

#: main.cpp:50
msgid "The version of the program"
msgstr "Programmverschoon"

#: main.cpp:51
msgid "The bug address to use"
msgstr "De Fehleradress, de brukt warrn mutt"

#: main.cpp:52
msgid "Translated name of the program"
msgstr "Översett Programmnaam"

#: main.cpp:53
msgid "The PID of the program"
msgstr "De Programm-PID"

#: main.cpp:54
msgid "Startup ID of the program"
msgstr "De Start-ID vun't Programm"

#: main.cpp:55
msgid "The program was started by kdeinit"
msgstr "'kdeinit' hett dat Programm start"

#: main.cpp:56
msgid "Disable arbitrary disk access"
msgstr "Egenmächtig Diskettentogreep ünnerbinnen"

#: main.cpp:71
msgid "The KDE Crash Handler"
msgstr "KDE Afstörten-Pleeger"

